      "writtenOn": "2023-08-31T19:24:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In many cases the when you create or update files the OS will cache those updates to write them more efficiently later. `sync` tells the OS to write all cached updates to disk now. This ensures that the file is already written if we do something like a hard power down (not rebooting, which would write cached updates) of the DUT right after creating the file.",
      "parentUuid": "14929856_295b0067",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 76,
        "startChar": 3,
        "endLine": 76,
        "endChar": 23
      },
